**/.ipynb_checkpoints
**/__pycache__
*.png
*.mp4
*.npy
*.npz
*.dae
# roar state — the generated setup stage runs `roar init`, which creates
# .roar/. Without this rule the worktree goes dirty and the FIRST PAID
# `roar run` refuses to execute ("Run blocked: untracked files").
.roar/
# --- reproduction outputs (scaffold_row.py: the "mnist rule") ---
# File-pattern ignore of each output dir plus a TRACKED .gitkeep, so the dir
# survives a clean checkout and roar keeps its outputs in lineage. Never
# dir-ignore. Upstream already carried `data/*` and `logs/*`; the negations and
# the nested rule for logs/<expname>/ are this fork's only change to this file,
# and a re-included directory must be listed BEFORE the pattern that would
# exclude its contents, or git never descends into it.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
!logs/blender_paper_lego/
logs/blender_paper_lego/*
!logs/blender_paper_lego/.gitkeep
